{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "label": "Chapter 12C \u2014 Time, and the clock in the constraint", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_clock_is_occupancy", "label": "The clock is occupancy, and the tick is k \u2212 g", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Occupancy never rises along composition, so the object graph falls into three strata pure in occupancy with full circulation inside each and no return between them."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_definability_not_reachability", "label": "Definability is not reachability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The lattice says what a cell is; composition says what it can become. Only 0.4% of ordered pairs are joined both ways, so a cell can be fully defined and unreachable."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_arrow_frame_dependence", "label": "The arrow is real, and it is a property of a frame", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "g carries two readings the construction does not distinguish \u2014 electrons placed and electrons present \u2014 which coincide only when the destination begins empty. Represent both and the index is equally lawful and equally closed at 13,775 cells, but 31.6% of composable pairs raise occupancy. Observation selects the frame, and the arrow is real within the one it selects."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_one_arrow_per_coordinate", "label": "One arrow per coordinate and no others", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An index does not have a clock; it has one per coordinate, and occupancy is the most restrictive of the four."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_arrow_decay_theorem", "label": "The decay theorem \u2014 arrow agreement is bounded by a quantity falling with tree distance", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The coordinates form a Markov random field on the tree, so conditioning on a separating vertex gives exact conditional independence and Pinsker bounds the overlap. The hypothesis is separation: give the graph a cycle and the bound has nothing to bound."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_past_present_future_path", "label": "Past \u2014 present \u2014 future is a path, not a triangle (treewidth 1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Treewidth 1 closes exactly and treewidth 2 gives an envelope, so \u039b's exactness is a proof that the three parts are not a triangle."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_future_conditionally_independent", "label": "The future is conditionally independent of the past given the present", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The past constrains only which presents are reachable; having spent that, it has spent everything. The future set is saturated and nests increasing while the past set nests decreasing."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_tick_decomposition", "label": "The tick decomposes \u2014 k \u2212 g = (k \u2212 q) + (q \u2212 g)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two independent sources of irreversibility contributing identically: a choice not taken and a capacity that could not receive. The arrow here is overwhelmingly a counting phenomenon, not a Pauli one."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_rev_lambda9_groupoid", "label": "rev(\u039b\u2089) and the timeless core \u2014 a 389-cell groupoid", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three of the four positions exist and the fourth does not: the union would need 2,857 further cells, so a structure holding both directions of time is not available at any price the index recognises."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_tower_table", "label": "Every \u039b in one table \u2014 E = 0 at every stage, fill falling 14.12% to 0.42%", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closure is the one property the tower never spends; each coordinate multiplies the box faster than it multiplies the object, so the tower admits more room and fills less of it."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_fourteenth_axis_bound", "label": "The fourteenth axis \u2014 bounded without being built", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fill is monotone decreasing by construction and bounded below by zero, so the sequence converges \u2014 a deduction. The stage-to-stage ratios are not monotone, so the value of the limit would come from the pattern and does not follow."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_empty_index_boundary", "label": "E(X) = 0 is necessary for completeness and not sufficient for content", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every closure test in the book passes on the empty index; what distinguishes \u039b is its seventeen generators and its seven bits of surplus."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_index_into_larger_index", "label": "How an index enters a larger index \u2014 as a chain, and small", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A coordinate must be totally ordered, so only rank survives the promotion: 199,130 cells become 44 values and a transition stops being a function of its inputs and becomes an interval. Ignorance about this index is not evidence of another."}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_clock_is_occupancy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_definability_not_reachability", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_arrow_frame_dependence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_one_arrow_per_coordinate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_arrow_decay_theorem", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_chapter12c", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12c_time_past_present_future_path", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12C-time.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewr